the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{18}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the positive answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}.$\n\nKnowing that $tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{sin⁡\\theta }{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{5}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}\\right)}=\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{\\sqrt{7}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{\\sqrt{7}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{18\\cdot 7}}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{126}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19cd8750-e5e7-52ce-b115-cbd111d3d902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{390}}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510726} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba5953e-1bc3-52b3-949b-b1a3372ec514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{390}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510734} {:answer/id #uuid "dca87888-b247-5218-bd97-b52279791479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510746} {:answer/id #uuid "ed349bbe-0002-555d-b774-e4baa909f28c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{79}}{10}" 