/value "\\frac{25}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511707} {:answer/id #uuid "f13958bf-0d8f-555a-bf51-2bf79723a49b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511711} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd43435-b072-5f01-b302-1d59e6fd5742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbd43435-b072-5f01-b302-1d59e6fd5742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511713} :answer-field/id #uuid "21996560-b703-53d3-bfc5-aac31475eee5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd4c56b2-c037-5749-b1cc-f43f2eb74d1e" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a35a31ccce6ce9e50c386b920c8c4b0fecf23a4f29741e982dcd6c69bf38453c.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{5},$ use the Pythagorean identity to find $2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/09/0961629419accd50af36ce88aecafe33ea264d278d18d6f71c4aa4d76c06be97.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=cos⁡\\theta ,\\,y=sin⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{5}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\nsin⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =2-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{5}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =2-2{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{5}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & =2-2\\left(\\frac{13}{25}\\right) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{26}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our final answer is $2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{24}{25}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13fa977c-7ab9-5f02-9a0c-1946b173eb62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511917} {:answer/id #uuid "43c63a3e-8c7e-5f9c-bed5-8356fb6459df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{30}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511927} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9f5765-9e63-51b4-81f2-ac00398068a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511935} {:answer/id #uuid "715877e7-423a-52e2-ba4f-128b52c9eff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511942} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8b713e-6030-54a2-bb0e-99ba1fba2a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f9f5765-9e63-51b4-81f2-ac00398068a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511935} :answer-field/id #uuid "88b4427d-f2f1-571e-900c-ab2a00e3a774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19ee0877-fb33-5fe0-9855-c6ff1fa21c11" :question/problem "If $\\cos x=\\frac{1}{7},$ then $2\\cos (x-14\\pi )+2=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-7$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x=\\cos (x+2\\cdot (-7)\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x-14\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=\\frac{1}{7},$ then $\\cos (x-14\\pi )=\\frac{1}{7}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cos (x-14\\pi )+2 & =2\\left(\\frac{1}{7}\\right)+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f260668-83d5-5737-be7a-fcd41740577c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511934} {:answer/id #uuid "7534c7ed-b9b9-5a4e-b7cc-648e83cbe230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511943} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4eb6cc-0bc2-52a2-b07f-504b6d6ecb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511945} {:answer/id #uuid "c55cc9ed-9a42-5e6f-9fff-988edf9b714f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{34}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511967} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d21f26-67b9-5b1e-b9e7-725f74bfd9d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{76}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b4eb6cc-0bc2-52a2-b07f-504b6d6ecb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511945} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a37119-64a0-594b-a7bb-6f870c3ecc3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "24687af9-7fd4-5bfe-b0b9-67927f085480" :question/problem "If $\\cos x=\\frac{5}{7},$ then $-4\\cos (x+10\\pi )+2=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x=\\cos (x+2\\cdot 5\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x+10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=\\frac{5}{7},$ then $\\cos (x+10\\pi )=\\frac{5}{7}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\cos (x+10\\pi )+2 & =-4\\left(\\frac{5}{7}\\right)+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{7}+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0139c477-5e87-5d46-857f-1e644b941aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511912} {:answer/id #uuid "46197fe5-c4cc-5300-bd68-d98bdaf687a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{34}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511928} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1cee34-400f-5464-8d28-7c1491e7128e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511929} {:answer/id #uuid "55cde37a-dc3e-5fca-9ffe-050d8732e68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{144}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511932} {:answer/id #uuid "6d088897-13c5-5628-a11b-29a2e1cecba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{24}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46197fe5-c4cc-5300-bd68-d98bdaf687a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{34}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511928} :answer-field/id #uuid "51fd72b7-5534-5859-b921-0fbb2129cd60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b461b9cd-5fb6-5c5e-92ad-d98cc83a4b85" :question/problem "If $\\cos x=-\\frac{2}{11},$ then $6\\cos (x-16\\pi )-2=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-8$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x=\\cos (x+2\\cdot (-8)\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x-16\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=-\\frac{2}{11},$ then $\\cos (x-16\\pi )=-\\frac{2}{11}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cos (x-16\\pi )-2 & =6\\left(-\\frac{2}{11}\\right)-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{11}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{34}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511973 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dad7e2b-bae8-5d84-8c3f-6468b2dc4e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{230}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511915} {:answer/id #uuid "1fec70af-72b7-516d-888c-519ee25da87b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511923} {:answer/id #uuid "60d115bc-5abe-5b32-a617-3d115b680270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{46}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511936} {:answer/id #uuid "89c3b91e-4518-5d73-8f7f-7b8cf00f0714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{54}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511952} {:answer/id #uuid "d1481b75-880b-5cb5-95b2-1b161d8953b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1481b75-880b-5cb5-95b2-1b161d8953b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511970} :answer-field/id #uuid "05357ae5-599f-5855-8b16-bae2d424708e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e3eb5fc0-3045-5e5d-a8b1-a1ea5cfdb161" :question/problem "If $\\cos x=\\frac{2}{11},$ then $-5\\cos (x+4\\pi )+4=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x=\\cos (x+2\\cdot 2\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x+4\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=\\frac{2}{11},$ then $\\cos (x+4\\pi )=\\frac{2}{11}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cos (x+4\\pi )+4 & =-5\\left(\\frac{2}{11}\\right)+4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{11}+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{34}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "741fac4f-1236-55d2-8c70-cfc0af005c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512030} {:answer/id #uuid "d6570710-b647-565c-a2c9-8585a674a4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6570710-b647-565c-a2c9-8585a674a4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512068} :answer-field/id #uuid