he graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$” is true. At $x=0$, the function has value $\\cos 0=1$.\n\n- Statement “The function is zero at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$” is true. $\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=0$.\n\n- Statement “The function has a maximum value at $x=\\pi.$” is false. $\\cos(\\pi)=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00c23a39-a692-59f0-82d6-1e42aa201914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{214}{125}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512098} {:answer/id #uuid "587f7451-fccf-5637-a502-7b906ce3c5c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512303} {:answer/id #uuid "5c47d0b3-930f-5e0f-872b-04d2b1a8ab8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512313} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f54150-f261-5643-bee1-64de82d8bd4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{52}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512499} {:answer/id #uuid "b96bcde9-98d4-501d-9658-acfed2d6a463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{125}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96bcde9-98d4-501d-9658-acfed2d6a463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{125}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512545} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c5eaee8-55ac-56b1-9f8a-3b273fc778c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28314126-6eaa-5326-a420-9e962fb3a315" :question/math-academy-id "q-147950" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}({x}^{3}+y),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{14}{25}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{19}{15},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}({x}^{3}+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{5}y{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}+xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{5}y{[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{5}y[\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}y]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{2}{25}y+\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{25}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{15}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{52}{75}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{52}{75}-\\left(\\frac{14}{25}\\right)\\left(\\frac{19}{15}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a36bbdb-d7de-52bd-851d-e6bd6d33739c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512424} {:answer/id #uuid "a49377ee-551e-5cb2-a025-28a2082dd9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{161}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512487} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c9bf09-d22c-5175-8478-b7129d7b3be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512605} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d6b444-7189-5948-8da8-571f44e98958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512607} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2b176c-6cdb-59e7-ad44-08efb439d9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4c9bf09-d22c-5175-8478-b7129d7b3be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512605} :answer-field/id #uuid "df1e1d9e-0dc1-5725-b77d-a7edfadad3f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "57775fd5-4d0c-5406-bb3e-6af6db58e9c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-147945" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{13}{10}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{13}{10},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{16}y{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{4}+x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{16}y{[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{16}y[\\frac{32}{5}+2{y}^{3}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{2}{5}y+\\frac{1}{8}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{40}{y}^{5}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}-\\left(\\frac{13}{10}\\right)\\left(\\frac{13}{10}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{100}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6042c78b-71af-5276-80cf-ccdcb9284bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512329} {:answer/id #uuid "6614a67a-a7fe-55e2-be74-7e1ab3c9e3c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512343} {:answer/id #uuid "b10534f0-4c95-531e-94d6-ba5e4a60964c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512516} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fff638-a832-599c-b20d-b7725b1e8582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512578} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b61c9c-6858-5b2e-a66c-1ae788e691c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6614a67a-a7fe-55e2-be74-7e1ab3c9e3c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512343} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd07e78-dd69-5881-8015-dd32bee64dd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5359436-369e-5935-88c6-73a8053a9364" :question/math-academy-id "q-66526" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}$ as a power of $e$ (the base of the natural logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{1/2}}={e}^{-1/2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}\\right)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-1/2})\n$$\n\nThe natural logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-1/2})=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cb46238-0858-5e29-93f5-3b1abf6e8453" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{135(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512264} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc4c62d-f986-5b1e-8753-4ec4676a3b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512311} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d76ec8-e500-538c-8442-85b23edc88a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{135(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6d76ec8-e500-538c-8442-85b23edc88a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{135(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512535} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e6a7300-844d-5db4-8005-d85823b210da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512770} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9336c13e-c8cb-5577-898b-73fc979337d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512448} {:answer/id #uuid "9e473653-b9e6-5e7c-a302-54a5b439449d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512469} {:answer/id #uuid "dadc4114-78f9-5557-a713-9afe7cf481ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e473653-b9e6-5e7c-a302-54a5b439449d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512469} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5322b59-ac05-57c5-bebd-3ff95532c124" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b98de4ab-a079-5d39-b165-ba7998caa236" :question/math-academy-id "q-343834" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}+5y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)+{{field-2}}\\cdot sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)+{b}_{n}sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)+{b}_{n}sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{3}cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)) \\\\  & \\,+5(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)+{b}_{n}sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)) \\\\  & \\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{5{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}+5{a}_{n})cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}+5{b}_{n})sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the cosine and sine coefficients, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{a}_{0}}{2} &=0 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}+5{a}_{n} &=\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi } \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}+5{b}_{n} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nNext, from the third equation, \n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{15}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{15}\\right)\\frac{n\\pi }{3}+5{a}_{n}=\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=\\frac{135(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${b}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{n\\pi }{15}\\cdot \\frac{135(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{135(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}\\cdot cos\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)+\\frac{9(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}\\cdot sin\\,\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6edd5f67-1149-5905-9dfd-2531aac7d778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512362} {:answer/id #uuid "8efe1823-faf5-5f48-bcfa-08d5910e2be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512436} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4df0cb-ec84-5087-bbab-1841e915272d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512468} {:answer/id #uuid "caf882ed-b1ef-5c87-ab85-e0fb21914627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{96}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512588} {:answer/id #uuid "fb927e68-a451-56b0-abb4-b479e7119a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d4df0cb-ec84-5087-bbab-1841e915272d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512468} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2d1682f-7eb6-5691-9d8f-0cd7e762540d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf31f09e-0f29-56f8-9f97-abccd7a0062d" :question/math-academy-id "q-147844" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{7}{12}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{7}{12},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}y]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\left(\\frac{7}{12}\\right)\\left(\\frac{7}{12}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045cd87c-d9d1-532d-aaf6-272ff651af69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x}-\\frac{53}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513315} {:answer/id #uuid "4e9d8b78-f2c7-59dd-a78b-3a2dbe330678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x}-\\frac{43}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513323} {:answer/id #uuid "514d1ee9-6408-54c9-b576-c871936d4bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x}-\\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513324} {:answer/id #uuid "705d3630-82da-5da8-b521-7a6dca553275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{53}{5}({\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513329} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1d6843-0183-5a48-b97d-d2117faca25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{48}{5}({\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "514d1ee9-6408-54c9-b576-c871936d4bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x}-\\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513324} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b6f1336-c230-52e6-81b1-93f174e89492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5379f918-5294-52ae-93f7-06745b15ed19" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cdc072e751a3277879d9e94380a2baf8c6a66bfc0de5d1cf5d8073f833efcb45.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y={\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x}+c.$ Determine the value of $c$ and find the equation of the curve." :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote of $y={\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x}$ is $y=0.$ The vertical translation $y={\\left(\\frac{53}{4}\\right)}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-\\frac{48}{5}.$ Therefore, $c=-\\frac{48}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0154092a-c2af-5c1f-a1ee-745b44d022b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{39}{2}\\right)}^{x}+\\frac{23}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513314} {:answer/id #uuid "74484cd2-a2cd-5a5f-b11d-063b39edc536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{39}{2}\\right)}^{x}-\\frac{18}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513330} {:answer/id #uuid "ae578d2a-2322-5f39-b0a7-2bbdc04ccbe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{39}{2}\\right)}^{x}+\\frac{18}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513336} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ec4c2f-3554-5ec2-aea7-b4f66d10f6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{39}{2}\\right)}^{x}-\\frac{23}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513340} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e0a985-2eaf-5d31-bdfe-18c36480ce04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{39}{2}\\right)}^{x}+\\frac{28}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0ec